course: dictionary
lesson: 14336
title: Occasions: times and special events
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word occasions can mean times when something happens. «We visited the zoo on three occasions last summer.» Here occasions means times, so they went to the zoo three times. Count the times to check.
explain: Occasions can also mean special events, such as weddings, birthdays or parties. «Mum wore her best dress on special occasions.» The words special and best tell you these are events worth dressing up for.
explain: Occasion is also used in some formal phrases. «On occasion» means sometimes, so «On occasion, Dad lets me stay up late» means that Dad lets you stay up late now and then, not always. When you meet a new phrase, try a simple word in its place and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: An occasion is a time when something happens.
fact: «On occasion» means sometimes.
fact: Special occasions are events like weddings, birthdays and celebrations.
fact: «There is no occasion to worry» is formal language that means there is no reason to worry.
fact: To occasion something means to cause it, as in «The storm may occasion some delays.»
exercise: In «We visited the zoo on three occasions last summer», what does occasions mean? | Long, hot days | *Times when something happened | Tickets for the zoo | Animals that live in zoos
exercise: Which of these is a special occasion? | Brushing your teeth | Walking to school on Monday | *A birthday party | Tidying your bedroom
exercise: «On occasion, Dad lets me stay up late.» Copy the two words that mean sometimes. | Dad lets | *on occasion | stay up | late
test: In «There is no occasion to worry», what does occasion mean? | A tiny clock | A loud noise | *Reason | A party
test: In «The storm may occasion some delays to the trains», what does occasion mean? | To hide | To celebrate | *To cause | To stop
exam: Which phrase means sometimes? | *On occasion | Special occasions | On two occasions, exactly | Every single day
